{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the strong.</b> Powerful, and it is an adjective of the noun, for the noun is חֹסֶן." "<b>For tow.</b> It is what is shaken out from flax." "<b>For a spark.</b> Like sparks, and like it וְנוֹצְצִים כְּעֵין נְחֹשֶׁת קָלָל (Ezekiel 1:7). The meaning concerns the idols, that they would strengthen them lest they totter — [but] those who act [toward them] in their time of distress, because they did not save them, [others] will burn them and they too will be burned." "And this is the meaning of <b>and both shall burn together.</b> Like מַדּוּעַ לֹא יִבְעַר הַסְּנֶה (Exodus 3:3)." "<b>And none extinguishes.</b> And none helps."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:55.496999249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}